  "name": "levels/level-2-jcs-utf16-key-order",
  "description": "Level 2 (ORGANIZATION_VERIFIED) with an annotations object whose keys are the RFC 8785 §3.2.3 property-sorting example, including U+1F600 (outside the Basic Multilingual Plane) and U+FB33. JCS sorts keys by UTF-16 code units, which puts U+1F600 (surrogates D83D DE00) before U+FB33; a code-point sort reverses them. The registry signed the UTF-16 order, so a conforming verifier ACCEPTs, and a verifier that sorts by code point reconstructs a different signing input and reports a spurious SIGNATURE_INVALID.",
